  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"869\" data-end=\"1065\">\n<p data-start=\"871\" data-end=\"1065\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"871\" data-end=\"883\">Detected</strong>: Indicates the presence of an HRAS gene mutation. May be associated with various cancers such as <strong data-start=\"981\" data-end=\"1038\">head and neck squamous cell carcinoma, bladder cancer</strong>, or <strong data-start=\"1043\" data-end=\"1064\">thyroid carcinoma</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1066\" data-end=\"1155\">\n<p data-start=\"1068\" data-end=\"1155\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1068\" data-end=\"1084\">Not Detected</strong>: No pathogenic mutation found in the HRAS gene in the analyzed sample.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1066\" data-end=\"1155\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1159\" data-end=\"1168\">Note:</strong> Clinical correlation with histopathological findings and other molecular markers is recommended for management decisions.</span></li>\n</ul>",
